Subject: Bound the work of one render at MAX_RENDER_STEPS element visits

A <use> fan-out -- a group using one symbol ten times, inside a symbol
used ten times, and so on -- multiplies the drawing work by ten per level
while the document grows by a few lines: twenty levels in a kilobyte draw
10^20 shapes, and nothing interrupts plutosvg_document_render(). The depth
caps bound nesting, not breadth.

Count each render_element() call in the render context and stop at
MAX_RENDER_STEPS (one million). plutosvg_document_render() returns false
when the budget ran out, so the caller can tell a truncated picture from a
complete one; plutosvg_document_extents() returns what it measured.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §12, §18 Q2. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutosvg/source/plutosvg.c
